WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:04.700
Heartbroken Spider-Man fans have received
a little fatherly wisdom to help ease the

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:05.700
pain.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.040
Dominic Holland, comedian, author, and father
of Spidey actor Tom Holland, recently took

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.420
to his blog to offer up his thoughtful take
on the prospect of the beloved character potentially

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:18.970
exiting the Marvel Cinematic Universe following
an impasse between Marvel Studios and rights

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:20.570
holder Sony Pictures.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:24.440
The elder Holland reminded fans in his August
21st post that they likely haven't seen the

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.660
last of his son's Spidey, and that in the
end, the factor which likely precipitated

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:32.980
the split will be the same one that ensures
that their favorite hero returns to the screen:

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:33.980
money.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:38.219
"My eldest son is owned by the world now,
but he's kinda still my little lad and I have

00:00:38.219 --> 00:00:39.590
to look after him."

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:43.219
Holland explained that he'd been asked for
his take on the situation by multiple media

00:00:43.219 --> 00:00:45.019
outlets, but had politely declined.

00:00:45.019 --> 00:00:49.730
For his blog's readers, however, he felt compelled
to comment, and he betrayed just a touch of

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:53.170
scorn for the big Hollywood power players
who had failed to get a new deal done for

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.539
the fans, writing,

00:00:54.539 --> 00:00:57.120
"I have no inside track on such issues.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.289
But whatever is decided by the big suits at
these big Hollywood studios my hunch is that

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:02.359
the show will continue.

00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:07.080
Too much at stake and too many dollars riding
on it and besides, everyone wants the same

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.330
thing; namely, Spider-Man on large screens
keeping people safe and entertained.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:14.020
And with Tom in the suit, for the time-being
at least.

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:17.829
And in the years ahead, no doubt, with another
lucky young actor in the role."

00:01:17.829 --> 00:01:21.750
Just a day later, the self-described "friendly,
neighborhood father of Tom Holland" felt the

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:26.310
need to clarify his statement due to the deluge
of headlines which followed his initial post.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:30.650
He wrote that he held no animosity towards
either party, and he appeared slightly irked

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:35.060
at the possibility that such misrepresentations
of his comments could reflect poorly on his

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.060
son, writing,

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:37.290
"As I said in the post…

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:41.979
'I know nothing' and my only speculation remains,
that Spider-Man will go on saving people and

00:01:41.979 --> 00:01:42.979
keeping us all entertained.

00:01:42.979 --> 00:01:47.590
In fact, Tom Holland's dad has not even spoken
with Tom Holland since this seismic story

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:52.320
broke and he certainly is not taking any sides,
he is not calling for any boycotts and he

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.939
will not be storming any offices anytime soon.

00:01:54.939 --> 00:01:56.409
These headlines are just click bait.

00:01:56.409 --> 00:01:59.689
A salacious headline to create website traffic."

00:01:59.689 --> 00:02:03.270
Holland closed with a pointed parting shot
at those who would twist his words for clicks,

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:06.350
followed by a bit of characteristically British
self-effacing humor.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.570
The elder Holland wrote,

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:12.210
"[The misrepresentation] is shameful and not
something I would ever stoop to until I consider

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:15.950
that I posted a blog on the subject knowing
that it might increase traffic to my site…

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.470
So, am I any better?

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:18.470
Maybe not.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:22.269
But I am not so stupid that I would ever do
anything to compromise my family and involving

00:02:22.269 --> 00:02:26.230
myself in something so far above my pay grade
immediately springs to mind."

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:30.400
Spider-Dad is certainly taking the high road
here, and so far, his son has had no comment

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:31.450
on the matter.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:35.690
He's continued to post on social media without
making any mention of the split but if comments

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:40.250
he's made previously are any indication, he's
probably not too psyched about it.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.959
Consider Holland's words when asked about
the possibility of his Spider-Man meeting

00:02:42.959 --> 00:02:47.239
up with Tom Hardy's Venom, whose adventures
take place in the wholly distinct Sony Universe

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:49.320
of Marvel Characters, in 2017.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.560
"You know, I'd love to make a movie with Tom
Hardy, and if we ever got the chance to make

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:55.480
a Venom movie together, that would be super
cool.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.180
But his movie would have to take place in
the MCU, because I'm not giving up my ticket."

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.959
Well, Tom, it sadly appears that you may not
have a choice.

00:03:01.959 --> 00:03:05.240
But it also appears that your dear old Dad
raised you well, because you appear to be

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:08.090
approaching the situation with the same level
head that he is.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:11.989
It's a delicate matter, and immediately going
public with ill-chosen, poorly thought-out

00:03:11.989 --> 00:03:14.680
words would be… well, irresponsible.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:18.170
And as we all know, with great power comes
great responsibility.

